# Banking Transactions API — Sample Requests
# Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension (Ctrl+Shift+P → "REST Client")
# Click "Send Request" above any ### block to fire that request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

# ============================================================
# 🏥 Health check
# ============================================================

### Root — confirm the server is alive
GET {{baseUrl}}/

# ============================================================
# 💸 Create Transactions (POST /transactions)
# ============================================================

### 1. Deposit — Alice receives her paycheck
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-00001",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-ALICE",
  "amount":      2500.00,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "deposit"
}

###

### 2. Transfer — Alice pays Bob for freelance work
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-ALICE",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-BOB01",
  "amount":      350.00,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

###

### 3. Withdrawal — Bob takes cash out
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-BOB01",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-ATM01",
  "amount":      100.00,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "withdrawal"
}

###

### 4. Transfer in EUR — Alice gets paid by a foreign client
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-CLNT1",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-ALICE",
  "amount":      800.00,
  "currency":    "EUR",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

###

### 5. Transfer — Bob repays Alice (partial, cents included)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-BOB01",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-ALICE",
  "amount":      50.25,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

# ============================================================
# ❌ Validation Error Examples (should return 400)
# ============================================================

### Bad: negative amount
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-67890",
  "amount":      -50,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

###

### Bad: amount with too many decimals
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-67890",
  "amount":      19.999,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

###

### Bad: invalid account format (missing ACC- prefix)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "12345",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-67890",
  "amount":      100,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

###

### Bad: unsupported currency
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-67890",
  "amount":      100,
  "currency":    "XYZ",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

###

### Bad: same fromAccount and toAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount":   "ACC-12345",
  "amount":      100,
  "currency":    "USD",
  "type":        "transfer"
}

# ============================================================
# 📋 List Transactions (GET /transactions)
# ============================================================

### All transactions — no filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions

###

### Filter by account (sent or received)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-ALICE

###

### Filter by type
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?type=transfer

###

### Filter by date range (adjust dates to match your test data)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?from=2024-01-01&to=2026-12-31

###

### Combine filters — Alice's transfers only
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-ALICE&type=transfer

# ============================================================
# 🔍 Get a Single Transaction (GET /transactions/:id)
# ============================================================

### Replace the ID below with a real one from a previous POST response
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/REPLACE-WITH-REAL-ID

###

### 404 example — ID that doesn't exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ============================================================
# 💰 Account Balance (GET /accounts/:accountId/balance)
# ============================================================

### Alice's balance (run after creating the sample transactions above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE/balance

###

### Bob's balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-BOB01/balance

###

### 400 example — invalid account format
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/INVALID/balance

# ============================================================
# 📈 Account Summary (GET /accounts/:accountId/summary)
# ============================================================

### Alice's full activity summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE/summary

###

### Bob's summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-BOB01/summary

###

### Account with no transactions — returns zero counts, not an error
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-NEW01/summary

# ============================================================
# 💰 Simple Interest (GET /accounts/:accountId/interest)
# ============================================================

### Alice's interest: 5% annual rate over 30 days
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE/interest?rate=0.05&days=30

###

### Higher rate, longer term — 8% over 1 year (365 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE/interest?rate=0.08&days=365

###

### Bob's interest at 3.5% for a quarter (90 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-BOB01/interest?rate=0.035&days=90

###

### 400 — missing rate parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE/interest?days=30

###

### 400 — negative rate
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE/interest?rate=-0.05&days=30

###

### 400 — days is zero
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE/interest?rate=0.05&days=0

# ============================================================
# 📤 Export Transactions as CSV (GET /transactions/export)
# ============================================================

# ℹ️  Rate Limiting note
# Every response includes these headers so you can track your quota:
#   X-RateLimit-Limit:     100
#   X-RateLimit-Remaining: <requests left in this window>
#   X-RateLimit-Reset:     <Unix timestamp when the window resets>
#
# When you exceed 100 requests/minute from the same IP, the API responds
# with 429 Too Many Requests and a Retry-After header (seconds to wait).
# The window resets automatically — no action required on your part.

### Export all transactions as CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export?format=csv

###

### Export only Alice's transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export?format=csv&accountId=ACC-ALICE

###

### Export transfers only
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export?format=csv&type=transfer

###

### Export with combined filters — Alice's transfers in a date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export?format=csv&accountId=ACC-ALICE&type=transfer&from=2024-01-01&to=2026-12-31

###

### 400 — missing format parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export

###

### 400 — unsupported format
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export?format=xml
